2026-10-31 - Navigation entries, text colors, page starts at top

Navigation entries get a custom label and size (default: all as large as the
largest). The text editor can set text color and highlight colors. The page
now starts at the top of the browser window. Restart FHEM, then
set <CMS> rebuild.

S20 - Navigationspunkte: Größe und Beschriftung
S21 - Texteditor: Farben

2026-10-31 - Navigation widget, no header

The page header and device card are gone. The navigation is now a movable
widget (horizontal or vertical) shared by all pages; creating, renaming,
deleting and reordering pages moved into its dialog. Restart FHEM, then
set <CMS> rebuild.

S17 - Schlanke Seite ohne Kopfbereich
S18 - Navigations-Widget (Umsortieren per Ziehen und Ausblenden pro Seite folgen)

2026-10-31 - Resize images and tiles by dragging

Images get a drag handle (5 percent steps, ratio kept) instead of percent
buttons. In layout mode tiles can be resized with a corner handle or
Shift+arrow keys, and the grid fields are removed from the tile dialogs.

2026-10-31 - Add a preview button for the draft

The edit mode has a Vorschau button that opens the current draft as the
finished page (mode=preview) in a new window.

2026-10-31 - Open CMS links in a new browser window

CMS starten and Zeige Homepage now open in a new window or tab.

2026-10-31 - Make the view mode the default

index.html without parameters now shows only the finished homepage. The edit
mode needs ?mode=edit, which the CMS starten link sets.

2026-10-31 - Add draft and publish workflow

Editing now changes a draft (draft.json) instead of the live page. Zeige
Homepage keeps showing the live version until Veroeffentlichen publishes the
draft, which backs up the previous live version. New commands get draft,
get status, set draft, set publish and set discard.

2026-10-31 - Add a view mode link for the finished homepage

The device now shows CMS starten (edit mode) and Zeige Homepage, which opens
index.html?mode=view without header, toolbar and edit buttons.

2026-10-31 - Add WYSIWYG text editor and image upload

Text blocks are edited in a rich text editor (formatting, links, tables, images
with positioning). HTML is validated against a strict allowlist in the browser
and in the module. set <CMS> media uploads PNG, JPEG and GIF images (max 3 MiB),
get <CMS> media lists them.

2026-10-31 - Move tiles freely in the 12 column grid

The new Layout button lets tiles be dragged by mouse or touch, or moved with
the arrow keys. Overlapping tiles are pushed down and the layout is saved.

2026-10-31 - Offer backups as a dropdown for set restore

FHEMWEB now lists the 20 newest backups as choices for "restore".

2026-10-31 - Add user documentation and acceptance protocol

docs/ANWENDER.md covers installation, usage, securing FHEMWEB with allowed
and troubleshooting. dev-docs/ABNAHME.md records what was and was not tested.

2026-10-31 - Add backup restore dialog

A Backups button lists the saved configurations and restores the selected one
after confirmation. The current state is backed up before it is replaced.

2026-10-31 - Add purge command to delete a device's data

set <name> purge <name> removes the data folder (with backups) and the start
page of a device after an explicit name confirmation. Symlinks, foreign files
and pages without the module marker are refused.

2026-10-31 - Show stale and offline states and clean up on page hide

Keep the last values visible when a refresh fails and mark tiles as stale,
reload immediately after a reconnect, pause polling in hidden tabs and stop
timers and subscriptions when the page is hidden.

2026-10-31 - Add text widget, multiple pages and navigation

Add the markdown text widget with a safe built-in renderer, pages with hash
navigation (add, rename, delete) and a general "+ Widget" menu. Subscriptions
only cover the current page.

2026-10-31 - Add rebuild command and text widget schema

Add set rebuild and throttled start page refresh from the FHEMWEB link so new
frontend assets get a fresh cache token without a restart. Accept text widgets
with a markdown field in the config schema.

2026-10-31 - Fix device picker layout

Use fixed column widths so all picker columns fit and show the hit count in a
neutral color.

2026-10-31 - Add channel lookup and column filters to the device picker

Resolve thermostat readings across the main device and its channels, show the
room and parent device in the picker, and add a filter field per column.

2026-10-31 - Add cache busting to the generated CMS page

Version the stylesheet, entry script and all modules with a content hash and
regenerate module-owned index.html files when frontend assets change.

2026-10-31 - Add device picker popup to thermostat dialog

Replace the device input list with a modal popup showing name, alias and type
with search over all columns.

2026-10-31 - Add thermostat test widget and config commands

Add schema version 2 with widget ids and a thermostat widget, get/set commands
for config, backups and restore, and a thermostat tile with configuration dialog.

2026-10-31 - Add per-device config storage

Create fhem-cms-data/<device>/ with a validated config.json, timestamped
backups and restore support. Existing devices are upgraded on the next start.

2026-10-31 - Remove temporary FHEMWEB Inform probe

Remove the one-off transport test page after verifying WebSocket status updates.

2026-10-31 - Simplify FHEMWEB inform probe output

Show only device names and states in the read-only inform probe instead of
including the large rendered SVG markup in the event list.

2026-10-31 - Add FHEM room and direct CMS link

Assign new CMS devices to the FHEM CMS room and show a room-view link to the
device entry page.

2026-10-31 - Use device names in CMS URLs

Use the FHEM device name in the generated device directory and returned URL.
Also accept the FHEMCMS module type regardless of capitalization.
Keep device files when the FHEM device definition is deleted.
Place the device entry point directly at <device>/index.html; CMS pages belong
to the device's content structure, not to separate surface directories.

2026-10-31 - Initial fhem-cms test device and frontend

Add the FHEMCMS device module, generated test page, and shared frontend component.
Add repository-wide FHEM update controls and installation instructions.
